WORKFLOW:
1. Before repeating a technique, query ``list_notes(category="learnings", search="<technique>")``. Check the note's context before deciding whether it rules out the current attempt.
2. After a meaningful attempt, record what you tried and what happened with ``add_learning(technique="<short_slug>", context="<conditions and result>", outcome="<outcome>")``.
3. When resuming this session, use ``list_notes(category="methodology", tags=["progress"])`` to review your completed work.

Outcome values:
- ``dead_end``: proved ineffective under the recorded conditions. Locked.
- ``promising``: partial signal requiring more investigation.
- ``confirmed``: a verified result under the recorded conditions. Locked.
- ``unknown``: inconclusive. Prefer this when a result is uncertain.

Changing a locked outcome requires ``update_note(..., force=True)``. Do not mark an untested assumption as a dead end or a confirmed result.
